  "description": "We developed a mini-barcode based on the 12S rRNA gene to identify predator from scats in Tasmania.\u00a0\nTo test the sensitivity of our primers to detect low template DNA samples, we set up serial dilutions of six DNA extracts originating from museum samples, representing each of the six mammal predators that might be detected in Tasmania (Tasmanian devil, eastern quoll, spotted tail quoll, cat, dog and fox).",
