   },
   {
    "id": 575993,
    "guid": "A03D2E7908354291927BE1625264D947",
    "previous_id": 575992,
    "previous_guid": "F1EFF17AF7954F68B1CAF71A8B9B622E",
    "section": "Set up 10 x dilutions",
    "section_color": null,
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "set up a series of six 10 X dilutions from each of these \u201cundiluted\u201d (90 ng / \u00b5l) samples\nfrom\u00a090 ng / \u00b5l to\u00a00.09 pg/\u00b5l",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 6534,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "2",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 575994,
    "guid": "2CC6CF86BB8F485585ED392CC5601F0B",
    "previous_id": 575993,
    "previous_guid": "A03D2E7908354291927BE1625264D947",
    "section": "qPCR replicates",
    "section_color": null,
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "For each dilution of each sample, perform three qPCR replicates (on a Viia7 Real-Time PCR system (Thermo Fisher Scientific)) : total volume of 25\u00b5l including 1X Gold buffer (Applied Biosystems), 2 mM MgCl2, 0.4 mg / ml BSA, 0.4 \u00b5M of each primer, 0.6 \u00b5l SYBR green (1:2000 Life Technologies nucleic acid gel stain), 0.25 mM of each dNTP, 1 unit of AmpliTaq GoldTM (Applied Biosystems) and 2 \u00b5l of the appropriate DNA dilution.\n \nqPCR protocol:\u00a0initial step of 95 \u00b0C for 5 mins; followed by 40 cycles of 95 \u00b0C for 30 s, 57 \u00b0C for 30 s and 72 \u00b0 for 30 s.",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 6534,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "3",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 575995,
    "guid": "D2BDDF6A09844BB49B1AF811D73F6473",
    "previous_id": 575994,
    "previous_guid": "2CC6CF86BB8F485585ED392CC5601F0B",
    "section": "Comparative CT analysis",
    "section_color": null,
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Using the ViiA7 software v1.2.4 with a threshold of 5,000 \u2206Rn, conduct a comparative CT analysis by calculating the mean CT value and the standard deviation across qPCR replicates for each dilution of each DNA sample.\nEvaluate to which dilution the mini-barcode is effective.",
    "data": null,
